## Architecture (required)

- **Hub:** Agency config Sheet — active accounts, **goal source of truth** (budgets / lead goals / Target CPL), client spoke Sheet URLs, alert recipients
- **Engine:** MCC Google Ads Script — `executeInParallel`, **Hub→Spoke goal sync**, GAQL extraction, write metrics to spokes
- **Spokes:** One isolated Sheet per client — green Hub-synced goal copies + yellow local monitoring + Search vs PMax daily metrics (Search keywords; PMax campaigns only) + weekly location/device roll-ups
- Daily metrics tabs must include `(Daily)` in the **tab name** and in-tab title; weekly tabs use `(Weekly)`
- Do **not** include a Search Ad Group Metrics tab; use Search Keyword Metrics (Daily) instead of ad-group rollups
- Do **not** include a PMax Keyword Metrics tab or PMax Asset Group Metrics tab — PMax has no classic keywords; use PMax Campaign Metrics (Daily)
- Newest daily/weekly metric rows must sit directly under the header (older history is pushed down)

**Single source of truth:** humans edit goals only on the Hub. Never ask operators to maintain budgets/CPL in both Hub and spoke.

## Non-negotiable guardrails

- Use account timezone only (`AdsApp.currentAccount().getTimeZone()`) — never UTC for yesterday/pacing dates
- Safe-divide all derived metrics (CTR, CPC, CPL, pacing) — no NaN in Sheets
- Daily metrics every run; weekly geo/device segments only on the configured weekday
- Parallel spoke writes must not use a global script lock (different spokes); never overwrite formulas unsafely
- One account failure must not kill the batch — try/catch, log, alert managers
- Polish Sheets: frozen headers, currency/percent formats, clean readable layout
- **Tab order:** working / data tabs first; put **Instructions** and **Definitions** toward the end on Hub and spoke workbooks. On **spoke** workbooks, put **Daily Checklist** first, then metrics, then Instructions + Definitions, then **Config last**. On **Hub**, Instructions + Definitions stay last.
- **Instructions stay in sync with tabs:** whenever Hub or spoke tabs are added, renamed, removed, or their purpose changes, update that workbook’s Instructions tab so every tab is clearly explained for humans
- **Hub Definitions stay in sync with Config columns:** whenever a Hub Config column is added, renamed, or its meaning changes, update `CONFIG_COLUMN_DEFINITIONS` in `create-hub-workbook.gs` (Definitions tab is generated from that map, in Config order). Write definitions in plain language with examples (easy for a non-expert to understand).
- **Spoke Definitions stay in sync with all tabs/columns:** whenever spoke Config keys or metrics headers change, update `buildSpokeDefinitionRows_()` in `create-body-shop-workbook.gs`. Group by tab; plain language + examples.
- Hub Instructions + Definitions: keep grid lines visible (`setHiddenGridlines(false)`)
- Hub Config: freeze only Account ID + Account Name (not a wide frozen pane that splits the sheet)

## Agent split

- **Ads Script agent:** Engine, GAQL, pacing, parallelism, timezone, errors
- **Sheets agent:** Hub schema, spoke structure, tab layout, routing
- **Sheet formatting agent:** Visual polish and formatting of spoke dashboards

Follow `docs/Read this to understand the Hub Engine and Spoke sheets - system blueprint.md` for Hub CONFIG columns, spoke tabs (Search vs PMax separated; weekly Location/Device), and Engine module ownership. Follow `docs/Read this for the technical plan to scale past 50 accounts with one Hub and one Engine.md` for sharding: cap parallel at 50, auto-advance a daily due queue, stamp `Last Successful Run` — do not create a new script or Hub per 50 shops.

**Forbidden:** Do not create one shared Google Sheet that dumps every client’s campaign/keyword metrics together. Hub = control plane only; Spokes = per-account dashboards only.
